{{nihongo|'''Harujima'''|春島|Harujima|extra=lit. "Spring Island"}} is the northernmost of the three primary [[w:Island|islands]] that constitute the [[w:Archipelago|archipelago]] of the Imperial Kingdom of Okaiken. Cartographically, the island forms one of the two northern branches of the archipelago's characteristic "Y-shape," extending north from the island of Yagikoshu. Distinguished by its [[w:Tropical climate|tropical climate]] and rugged [[w:Topography|topography]], Harujima serves as the strategic, political, and cultural anchor of the nation, housing the national capital, [[Okami]], and the Wisteria Throne.

As one of the "Three Lands" ({{nihongo|三国|Sankoku}}) that define modern Sanese identity, Harujima contains a significant portion of the nation's 63,140-square-mile core landmass. It transitioned from the site of the archipelago's earliest prehistoric [[w:Human migration|migrations]] to the modern seat of the "Functional Royalty" following the Jutsu Restoration of 2011. Its role as the administrative heart of the state is characterized by extreme [[w:Population density|population density]] in its coastal plains, necessitated by a mountainous interior that restricts [[w:Arable land|arable land]] to less than 18% of the total area.

== Etymology ==
The name "Harujima" is a modern standardized identifier that functions as part of the broader ''Sankoku'' ("Three Lands") strategy employed by the central government. Historically, the archipelago was referred to by various [[w:Exonym and endonym|exonyms]], most notably Mitoyagi. However, a 1971 technocratic rebranding under Prime Minister Yoshimizu Ohno sought to dissolve insular tribalism and historical divisions.

By categorizing the northern tropical island as "Spring Island," the central hub as "Stone Island" (Ishijima), and the southern reaches as "Yagikoshu," the state fostered a unified Sanese ({{nihongo|三人|Sanjin}}) identity. This shift from regional identifiers to a unified [[w:Demonym|demonym]] was a deliberate socio-political strategy intended to break from the [[w:Feudalism|feudal]] legacy of the ancient "Mito" lineage and embrace a nomenclature reflecting the unified, technocratic nature of the modern state.

== Geography and Topography ==
=== Physical Characteristics ===
Harujima is a topographically rugged island defined by high [[w:Mountain range|mountain ranges]] and deep, fertile [[w:Valley|valleys]]. The island's interior is dominated by the Harujima Alps, a massive system of intersecting ridges that form the highest belt of mountains in the nation. The coastline is exceedingly irregular, particularly along the Katsuran Sea to the north, which features numerous navigable [[w:Inlet|inlets]] and natural [[w:Harbor|harbors]].

Due to the island's sharp, steep mountains, only 15 to 18 percent of Harujima is considered arable. This severe geological constraint has forced the vast majority of the population to settle in two primary level regions: the Kinai Plain, containing the city of Minamisanroku, and the Sendai Plain, the site of the sprawling Okami metropolitan area.

=== Major Rivers ===
The island's hydrology is defined by fast-flowing rivers that descend rapidly from the Harujima Alps, providing vital resources for both agriculture and modern industry.

