== Infrastructure and Economy ==
=== Transportation ===
Harujima possesses a highly automated and efficient [[w:Transport|transportation network]]. The Harujima [[w:High-speed rail|Shinkansen]] connects the northern metropolis with the rest of the archipelago, facilitating the daily movement of millions of commuters. The national expressway system utilizes the "Oka-Pass"—a mandatory electronic toll and automated guidance system that optimizes traffic flow through the island's mountainous terrain. The island’s heavy maritime needs are served by Okami Port, while Okami-Tobu International Airport acts as the primary aviation gateway for the East Fosian Sphere.

=== Industrial Base ===
The island was the primary driver of the "Sanese Industrial Miracle." Following the Digital Infrastructure Act of 2008, the island's [[w:Economy|economy]] successfully shifted from heavy manufacturing to digital sovereignty and advanced computing. Harujima serves as the strategic home for Kizan Systems, the corporation providing the hardware backbone for the nationwide Satori [[w:Artificial intelligence|AI]] network. Under the state's "Technocratic Shield" doctrine, the island’s infrastructure is heavily subsidized and prioritized to ensure the absolute security of the nation's "Silicon Lanes."

== Flora, Fauna, and Tourism ==
Harujima’s [[w:Biodiversity|biodiversity]] ranges from subtropical moist [[w:Broadleaf forest|broadleaf forests]] in the lowlands to various [[w:Conifer|conifers]] in the higher alpine altitudes. The island is the historic home of the [[w:Chrysanthemum|Chrysanthemum]], the national flower and symbol of the Imperial House, as well as the Sanese [[w:Macaque|macaque]] (red-faced monkey). The macaques are a notable tourist attraction, particularly for their habit of bathing in volcanic [[w:Hot spring|hot springs]] during the cooler winter months in the high altitudes.

[[w:Tourism|Tourism]] on the island is defined by the ''Jutsu Hyakkei'' (Hundred Views), a state-sponsored registry that catalogs both natural landscapes and man-made landmarks. Reflecting the island’s modern identity, "Industrial Heritage" sites like the Sentoku Tower and the Great Seawall have become as vital to Harujima's tourism sector as its traditional shrines and temples. This seamless blend of ancient tradition and futuristic industry ensures Harujima's enduring role as the heart of the Sanese national psyche.

